msgid "Update projects to the latest Quarkus version"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can update or upgrade your {project-name} projects to the latest version "
"of {project-name} by using an update command."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The update command primarily employs OpenRewrite recipes to automate updates "
"for most project dependencies, source code, and documentation."
msgstr ""

msgid "This technology is considered {extension-status}."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In _experimental_ mode, early feedback is requested to mature the idea.\n"
"There is no guarantee of stability nor long term presence in the platform "
"until the solution matures.\n"
"Feedback is welcome on our https://groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-"
"dev[mailing list] or as issues in our https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"issues[GitHub issue tracker]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a full list of possible statuses, check our https://quarkus.io/faq/#what-"
"are-the-extension-statuses[FAQ entry]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The update command automates only a subset of the migration.\n"
"Always review the {quarkus-migration-guide} for your target version to "
"identify any additional steps that require manual changes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Post-update, if expected updates are missing, consider the following reasons:"
""
msgstr ""

msgid "The recipe might not include a specific item in your project."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your project might use an extension that is incompatible with the latest "
"{project-name} version."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

msgid "To complete this guide, you need:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Roughly {prerequisites-time}"
msgstr ""

msgid "An IDE"
msgstr ""

msgid "JDK 17+ installed with `JAVA_HOME` configured appropriately"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache Maven {maven-version}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally the xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] if you want to use it"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally Mandrel or GraalVM installed and xref:building-native-image."
"adoc#configuring-graalvm[configured appropriately] if you want to build a "
"native executable (or Docker if you use a native container build)"
msgstr ""

msgid "A project based on {project-name} version 2.13 or later."
msgstr ""

msgid "Procedure"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create a working branch for your project by using your version control "
"system."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To use the Quarkus CLI in the next step, xref:cli-tooling.adoc#installing-"
"the-cli[install the latest version of the Quarkus CLI].\n"
"Confirm the version number using `quarkus -v`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Go to the project directory and update the project to the latest stream:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Using Quarkus CLI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optional: To specify a particular stream, use the `--stream` option; for "
"example: `--stream=3.2`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Using Maven"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optional: To specify a particular stream, use the `-Dstream` option; for "
"example: `-Dstream=3.2`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Analyze the update command output for potential instructions and perform the "
"suggested tasks if necessary."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use a diff tool to inspect all changes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Review the {quarkus-migration-guide} for your target version and apply any "
"additional steps not covered by the update command."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Ensure the project builds without errors, all tests pass, and the "
"application functions as required before deploying to production."
msgstr ""

msgid "Update recipes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The OpenRewrite recipes used by the update command are maintained in the "
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus-updates[Quarkus Updates] repository.\n"
"If you find that a recipe is missing or incorrect, you can contribute "
"improvements there.\n"
"Refer to the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus-updates/blob/main/README."
"md[README.md] and the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus-updates/blob/main/"
"CONTRIBUTING.md[CONTRIBUTING.md] guide for detailed instructions on how to "
"write and test recipes."
msgstr ""
